      "writtenOn": "2026-08-06T14:42:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My concern is from textbook point of view, casting signed integer into unsigned, there is  risk of underflow. I know POSIX error codes like ENOENT\u003d2, EACCES\u003d13, EIO\u003d5 are positive so chances of rollover are less in this scenario, but just pointing it out to see if we can avoid such conversions.\n\nAs discussed, we can live with this for now.",
      "parentUuid": "1013c993_7240a29e",
      "revId": "a47424aaead35304c9d11faf418fa3bf7e1a8614",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
